{
  "id": "s04-l02",
  "unit": "s04-conjuncts",
  "title": "Conjuncts 2: doubled letters",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "When the same consonant is written twice, Bengali stacks it, and you **hold the sound longer**: আম্মু (`ammu`, *mom*) is *am-mu*, বাচ্চা (`bachcha`, *child*) is *bach-cha*.\n\n**ম্ম** and **ল্ল** look like two copies squeezed together (চল্লিশ `chollish`, *forty*). **ন্ন** stacks one ন on another (রান্না `ranna`, *cooking*). **চ্চ** puts a small চ on top of another.\n\n**চ্ছ** is চ + ছ, a held `ch` with a puff: শুভেচ্ছা (`shubhechchha`, *best wishes*).\n\nDoubling matters in Bengali; saying it short can sound like a different word or just 'foreign'. Clap twice for a double letter while you practise.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "cj-mmo",
      "bn": "ম্ম",
      "tr": "mmo",
      "en": "double m (ম + ম)",
      "notes": "ম U+09AE + ্ + ম. আম্মু ammu. আব্বু uses the same idea with ব্ব."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-chcho",
      "bn": "চ্চ",
      "tr": "chcho",
      "en": "double ch (চ + চ)",
      "notes": "চ U+099A + ্ + চ. বাচ্চা bachcha."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-chchho",
      "bn": "চ্ছ",
      "tr": "chchho",
      "en": "ch + chh (চ + ছ), a held, puffed ch",
      "notes": "চ + ্ + ছ U+099B. শুভেচ্ছা shubhechchha; also in verb forms like করছি (said korchhi)."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-llo",
      "bn": "ল্ল",
      "tr": "llo",
      "en": "double l (ল + ল)",
      "notes": "ল U+09B2 + ্ + ল. চল্লিশ chollish; আলহামদুলিল্লাহ."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-nno",
      "bn": "ন্ন",
      "tr": "nno",
      "en": "double n (ন + ন)",
      "notes": "ন + ্ + ন. রান্না ranna. Sounds the same as য-ফলা on ন (ন্য in ধন্যবাদ), s04-l04: keep apart in listening tests."
    }
  ],
